# Document Titles (Web)

Browser tab titles use **`NetworthDB | <Action>`**. This rule applies to the web app document title — not Markdown headings (see the `markdown-title-case` rule).

## Component

Use [`PageTitle`](../../src/apps/web/src/components/Layout/PageTitle.tsx) from `@web/components/Layout/PageTitle`:

```tsx
import { PageTitle } from "@web/components/Layout/PageTitle";

export default function CategoriesPage() {
  return (
    <>
      <PageTitle page="Categories" />
      {/* ... */}
    </>
  );
}
```

- **Home / default** — `<PageTitle />` or omit `page` for plain `NetworthDB` (match `html.title` in Rsbuild config when set).
- **Action** — short page label in **title case** (`Sign In`, `Page Not Found`, `Account Details`).

```tsx
// BAD
<PageTitle page="sign in" />
<PageTitle page="account recovery" />

// GOOD
<PageTitle page="Sign In" />
<PageTitle page="Account Recovery" />
```

For routes that cannot use React Helmet-style components, set `document.title` to the same pattern: `NetworthDB | Sign In`.
